The native YOLOX Burn model implementation in src/models/yolox was initially adapted from
tracel-ai/models/yolox-burn at revision ec1b9e42e6692ef2b95f85c4ba783e07cd3d19af.
That project is distributed under the MIT OR Apache-2.0 licenses; this derivative uses the
Apache-2.0 option (LICENSE-APACHE).

The YOLOX architecture and COCO pretrained model originate from Megvii's YOLOX project:
https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX
The original implementation and pretrained weights are distributed under Apache-2.0.

The experimental src/models/yolov3_tiny, src/models/yolov10, and src/models/yolo26 implementations
interoperate with the public YOLOv3-Tiny-Ultralytics, YOLOv10n, and YOLO26n architectures and
official checkpoints. They were authored as native Burn code; boquilens does not bundle Ultralytics
Python code or model weights. tools/export_ultralytics_state.py and the per-model
export_*_fixtures.py scripts use an installed Ultralytics package at conversion time to extract
tensor state from a checkpoint.
Ultralytics states that its software, architectures, and trained model weights are offered under
AGPL-3.0 by default, with separate commercial licensing available:
https://www.ultralytics.com/license
Because boquilens is AGPL-3.0, checkpoints and the derived native artifacts may be redistributed
under the same license. Users supplying or publishing an Ultralytics checkpoint remain responsible
for satisfying the license applicable to that model and their use case.

